<h3 style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&=
quot;,sans-serif">Case 3: Bayes-envelope exact form</span><o:p></o:p></h3>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">The exact general object may not be a sim=
ple scalar
</span><img border=3D"0" width=3D"29" height=3D"38" style=3D"width:.3in;hei=
ght:.4in" id=3D"_x0000_i1112" src=3D"cid:image123.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"><s=
pan style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">=
. It may be:</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;margin-bottom:12.0p=
t;line-height:15.0pt">
<img border=3D"0" width=3D"370" height=3D"30" style=3D"width:3.85in;height:=
.3166in" id=3D"_x0000_i1111" src=3D"cid:image124.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"><o:=
p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">This is the cleanest exact expression.</s=
pan><o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">Then mutual information becomes the compr=
essive summary or upper bound.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">That gives you a hierarchy:</span><o:p></=
o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;margin-bottom:12.0p=
t;line-height:15.0pt">
<img border=3D"0" width=3D"208" height=3D"18" style=3D"width:2.1666in;heigh=
t:.1833in" id=3D"_x0000_i1110" src=3D"cid:image125.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"><=
br>
<img border=3D"0" width=3D"427" height=3D"18" style=3D"width:4.45in;height:=
.1833in" id=3D"_x0000_i1109" src=3D"cid:image126.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"><o:=
p></o:p></p>
<div class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"center" style=3D"text-align:center;line-h=
eight:15.0pt">
<span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif=
">
<hr size=3D"2" width=3D"100%" align=3D"center">
</span></div>
<h2><span style=3D"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">6. Fifth up=
grade: connect to Blackwell informativeness</span><o:p></o:p></h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">This is where the paper becomes more cont=
rol/information-theory mature.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">Mutual information is not a complete orde=
ring of information structures. Two observations can have the same mutual i=
nformation but different usefulness for a particular
 decision problem. So the strongest formal framework is probably:</span><o:=
p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;margin-bottom:12.0p=
t;line-height:15.0pt">
<img border=3D"0" width=3D"58" height=3D"18" style=3D"width:.6083in;height:=
.1833in" id=3D"_x0000_i1108" src=3D"cid:image127.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"><o:=
p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">meaning
</span><img border=3D"0" width=3D"14" height=3D"38" style=3D"width:.1416in;=
height:.4in" id=3D"_x0000_i1107" src=3D"cid:image128.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"=
><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-seri=
f">is Blackwell more informative than
</span><img border=3D"0" width=3D"14" height=3D"38" style=3D"width:.1416in;=
height:.4in" id=3D"_x0000_i1106" src=3D"cid:image129.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"=
><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-seri=
f">. Then:</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;margin-bottom:12.0p=
t;line-height:15.0pt">
<img border=3D"0" width=3D"194" height=3D"18" style=3D"width:2.0166in;heigh=
t:.1833in" id=3D"_x0000_i1105" src=3D"cid:image130.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"><=
o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">for all utilities
</span><img border=3D"0" width=3D"11" height=3D"38" style=3D"width:.1166in;=
height:.4in" id=3D"_x0000_i1104" src=3D"cid:image131.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"=
><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-seri=
f">.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">Then mutual information becomes a scalar =
relaxation:</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;margin-bottom:12.0p=
t;line-height:15.0pt">
<img border=3D"0" width=3D"124" height=3D"18" style=3D"width:1.2916in;heigh=
t:.1833in" id=3D"m_-8563055473070816419_x005f_x0000_i1025" src=3D"cid:image=
132.png@01DD19E9.0FB00090"><o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">does not always imply Blackwell dominance=
, but it often gives useful bounds.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">This would make your upgraded theory more=
 defensible:</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:15.0pt"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;font-family=
:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif">The exact control value is governed by th=
e decision value of the delayed information structure; mutual information g=
ives a universal scalar upper bound and a closed-form
 equality in symmetric binary admission.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
